index 0000000..f4143ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PERFORMANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+The homepage automatically measures clicks on navigation links, Order Now, and
+Seasonal Favorites cards (including their View Details links). Delegation also
+covers cards inserted later, without changing link behavior.
+
+Read the latest 100 samples with `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getSamples()` or
+subscribe to `window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => …)`.
+Samples contain `kind`, a stable `label`, a unique `id`, `startTime`, `duration`
+(milliseconds), and `method`. A User Timing measure is also delivered to any
+PerformanceObserver observing `measure` entries; entries are immediately cleared
+to avoid accumulating browser performance records. No data is sent off-device.
+
+This static page has no client-side router or view switches. When adding one,
+wrap its actual render operation:
+
+```js
+await window.dailyGrindPerformance.measureViewSwitch('menu', async () => {
+  const menu = await loadMenu();
+  renderMenu(menu);
+  // If the renderer commits asynchronously, await its commit here too.
+});
+```
+
+Each measurement ends in a task scheduled from requestAnimationFrame, allowing
+the visual update to paint first. This is an **after-paint estimate**, not an
+exact compositor timestamp or the INP metric. The technique follows the
+[web.dev rendering guidance](https://web.dev/articles/optimize-inp).
+Click durations include input delay when a usable event timestamp is available.
+View-switch durations include the callback's asynchronous work. These timings
+cover the next paint after the update, not the completion of subsequent CSS
+animations or images loading after the callback resolves.
+
+Regular links still perform full-document navigation. A click sample measures
+only the current document's response; it cannot measure the destination page's
+paint. Pending measurements are discarded when the document hides or leaves,
+and failed view switches produce no success sample. For destination-page load
+timing, instrument those pages separately. Async view switches should use the
+helper above rather than treating their click sample as render completion.
